      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies that a `Tag` obtained via `Tag.valueOf(\"I\")` (from the TagSet, thus \"known\") is NOT equal to a `Tag` created directly via `new Tag(\"I\")` (not in TagSet, thus not known), even though they share the same name, namespace, and normalName. Let me write the improved version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated names (`tag0`, `tag1`, `boolean0`) with descriptive ones (`knownItalicTag`, `standaloneItalicTag`, `tagsAreEqual`), adds a Javadoc comment explaining the core scenario, and annotates each assertion with a comment clarifying the WHY — all without changing any method calls, arguments, or expected outcomes."
